{
  "title": "MediaAudio",
  "description": "Audio played through the browser's media pipeline from an `HTMLAudioElement`, shared by Music and AudioStream. Memory scales with the decode buffer rather than the duration. It holds the element and default playback parameters but does not play itself: `audio.play(media, options)` returns a voice for pause, resume, seek, loop, rate, volume and spatial control. An element has a single playhead, so there is **one active voice at a time** - playing again stops the previous voice. Playback routes through the `music` bus by default. Use Sound for short, frequently triggered clips that benefit from a decoded `AudioBuffer` and overlapping playback.",
  "symbol": "MediaAudio",
